        "ratings": [
            {
                "comment": "Professor Bernault led very interesting discussions. However, I felt like she had more to say about my writing style than the actual content of my work. As a history major, I've worked incredibly hard on refining my historical writing style. For this class, I had to pretty much chuck everything out the window and adapt my style to what she wanted.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 3
            },
            {
                "comment": "She is a very nice person outside of class, but if you constantly use passive voice in your writing, or have super long sentences, expect to be marked down 10% on each of your writing submissions. She is a very big stickler on style, so you need to make sure that your writing is impeccable, and even then there may be issues.",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 3
            },
            {
                "comment": "She is absolutely wonderful. I would love to have her again as a professor. She really cares about her students and she's the only teacher I've had so far that knows my name. She loves seeing kids getting involved in class and going to office hours.GO TO OFFICE  HOURS! Loved her, but material is a little difficult since there's so much to remember!",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
